# 13. Deliverables

## Purpose

Project deliverables define the principal engineering outputs that shall be produced, maintained, and governed throughout the lifecycle of the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA) project.

These deliverables represent the tangible outcomes of the project's engineering activities and collectively form the AVIA Engineering Knowledge Base.

---

## Primary Deliverables

### PD-001 — Engineering Repository

A governed engineering repository that preserves, organizes, and maintains all approved engineering knowledge generated by the project.

---

### PD-002 — Project Charter

The official document establishing the purpose, objectives, scope, governance, and engineering philosophy of the AVIA project.

---

### PD-003 — System Objective Specification (SOS)

A formal specification defining the objectives that the engineered system is required to achieve.

---

### PD-004 — System Requirements Specification (SRS)

A structured specification translating system objectives into verifiable engineering requirements.

---

### PD-005 — Engineering Architectures

A collection of engineering architectures describing the functional, physical, mathematical, control, mechanical, electrical, and decision structures of the AVIA system.

---

### PD-006 — Engineering Analyses

Scientific analyses, engineering studies, mathematical models, simulations, and supporting technical evaluations used to investigate and validate engineering concepts.

---

### PD-007 — Validation and Verification Evidence

Engineering reports, simulations, test results, reviews, and other evidence demonstrating that engineering objectives and requirements have been satisfied.

---

### PD-008 — Engineering Knowledge Assets

Engineering principles, design guidelines, technical references, glossaries, methodologies, and other reusable knowledge developed during the project.

---

## Deliverable Governance

All project deliverables shall:

- Be uniquely identified.
- Be version controlled.
- Undergo engineering review before approval.
- Maintain traceability to project objectives and system requirements.
- Be preserved within the governed engineering repository.

---

## Engineering Perspective

The primary deliverable of the AVIA project is not only an adaptive vehicle architecture but also a comprehensive, traceable, and reusable body of engineering knowledge capable of supporting future research, development, validation, and implementation.
